  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-31T20:49:55.278Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be cool if something was added to the SDK that allows a user to make their avatar interactable by other players. As an example, a user could add a trigger that can be activated by other players. Another example would be the ability to push or even pick up an avatar.\n\nWhile this would make it easier to break collision in certain maps, a simple flag that disables such interactions within worlds would do fine.\n\nI feel that this would greatly expand the ways players can interact with other players in VRChat, adding another dimension of socializing.\n\nNote that this is specifically how other players interact with an avatar, not how one avatar can interact with other players. We don't want a player pushing other players around!",
